      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think there is no way to really fix this, either you sync it up using up performance or you don't. The way it is right now also works around another issue with colliders that has been making ragdolls incredibly hard and hacky to implement. Since mirror copys no longer update while no mirror is around, it is technically not required anymore to do some branching path shenanigans to prevent the mirror copy from enabling colliders too (causing colliders to collide with their mirror/real counterpart and freaking the physics out)... at least for as long as no mirror is around that is.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
